At  9:50 PM 7/23/94 -0400, Reilly Jones wrote:
>Lao Tzu                 (605)      China         Religious Leader

There is doubt about whether Lao Tzu was a single person, or a mythical
author for a collection of verses that have diverse authors and origins
(translation of Lao Tzu = Old Man). His (mythical?) occupation was
wanderer, hermit, etc., but not religious leader. One might as well call
him an early scientist - the distinction between religion, philosophy, and
science would not have meant much to the people of that time and place. He
didn't claim that any supernatural beings accosted him in the form of a
burning bush with instructions for proper behavior.

