After reading your post, it seems to me that the problem is not so
much developing an extropian medical ethics as it is either (a) to
convince other people that extropian medical ethics is indeed ethical
or (b) to prevent their disagreement on this point from interfering
with our own efforts to secure our own health and further our own
development.

The Harry-Browne types would go with option (b), of course.

