I'm just wondering, but has anyone else been reading
the Wall Street Journal regarding current events in
Venezuela?

I have a recent article scanned in, and will transfer it to my account
as soon as the relevant machine is free.  I would appreciate it if
someone would advise me on whether I can forward it to extropians
without permission. (I think so). I'd also like comments on whether I
can forward it to cypherpunks without having to get written
permission, or how to gain such permission in a timely manner.

The long and the short of it is, despite all the hoopla about the
victory of capitalism, Venezuela is becoming what is essentially a
communist state.

Some questions: does the dominance of the Venezuelan economy by a
single industry (the oil industry, plus some mining on the side; the
aluminum refining can be considered a subset of the energy industry),
coupled with its severe dependance on external trade, make the
transition, any recoveries to a more normal state, and the aftermath
much worse?

Did the fact that Venezuela was essentially a "company town" make a
socialist/communist takeover more likely?

What parts of the United States (beyond Louisiana, which in a way is
the most obvious example I can think of, and before you ask, no, I
don't think I'd change that answer if I didn't live here) are most
like Venezuela in relying on one or a few industries for there
economic liveleihood?

Is what is happening in Venezuela a possible "dress-rehersal" for the
United States? (This question could also apply to the last 40 years of
the history of the Phillipines).

Are there any near-term (say 3 to 6 months) ways to use
crypto-anarchic technologies to help the situation? It seems to me
that many businessmen there will be in the market for whatever
Chaumian schemes are in existance now, although there also seems to me
to be the problem that there probably aren't any pre-existing
arrangements, currency stockpiles, or whatever to provide for an easy
conversion of assets, especially if you're already stuck with
Bolivars, into Chaumian assets.

If anyone reading this on the extropians list is also on the
cypherpunks list, I'd like to post it there, but I'm not on right now
